    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9b803b6e_191756b0",
        "filename": "apex/allowed_deps.txt",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 2,
      "author": {
        "id": 1061164
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-26T20:27:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We are propagating min_sdk_version attributes across the codebase and asking module owners to approve those. That covers part of the \"ownership\" problem, as people are now more aware.\n\nWe\u0027ll have to populate the whitelist somehow regardless, whether we start with all these or add them individually later. I don\u0027t think we\u0027ll realistically get to the later before end of Q2. De-facto these modules are being tested today with all these dependencies already. New changes will be caught here and prevent regressions.\n\nre: combined list of deps vs per module deps:\n- If we decide to shard this file (see other comment), we\u0027ll end up with per module deps anyhow.\n- Significant chunk of the deps are non-overlapping, as this list only tracks static deps.\n- Seeing per module deps is also nice to know whether the static dependency is expected or not (size bloat and correctness issues).\nThe major downside of \"all individual deps of every module\" is that with sharded whitelist, library owners will be required to update multiple files in different projects. I don\u0027t have a good intuition of the flatness of the android build graph though: are most of the dep changes happen at top apex/apk level, or transitively by library owners?\n\nI expect Dario to also chime in on the format once I add more people to review. :-)",
      "parentUuid": "1c33b0bb_12b96409",
      "revId": "e4e1f2c64df58cd124461432a404543271b968ed",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
